.TH "DATEDIFF.SH" "1" "June 2026" "v0.30" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
.PP
\ \ \ \f[B]datediff.sh\f[R] \- Calculate time ranges / intervals between
dates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\ \ \ \f[B]datediff.sh\f[R] [\-Rrttuvvv] [\-\f[I]NUM\f[R]] [\-f
\f[I]\[dq]FMT\[dq]\f[R]] \f[I]DATE1\f[R] \f[I]DATE2\f[R]
[\f[I]UNIT\f[R]]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\ \ \ \f[B]datediff.sh\f[R] \f[B]\-FF\f[R] [\-v]
[[\f[I]DAY_IN_WEEK\f[R]] [\f[I]DAY_IN_MONTH\f[R]]]
[\f[I]START_DATE\f[R]]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\ \ \ \f[B]datediff.sh\f[R] \f[B]\-ee\f[R] [\-v] \f[I]YEAR\f[R]..
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\ \ \ \f[B]datediff.sh\f[R] \f[B]\-l\f[R] [\-v] \f[I]YEAR\f[R]..
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\ \ \ \f[B]datediff.sh\f[R] \f[B]\-m\f[R] [\-v] \f[I]DATE\f[R]..
.SH DESCRIPTION
Calculate the time interval (elapsed time) between \f[I]DATE1\f[R] and
\f[I]DATE2\f[R] in various time units.
.PP
Special functions include generating dates for Easter, Carnaval, and
Corpus Christi, checking for leap years, and generating moon phase
calendars.
.PP
Input is expected to be ISO\-8601 date or UNIX time.
However, the script can leverage an external \f[CR]C\-code date\f[R]
utility for robust parsing of diverse date formats.
